      "text": "We can visualize this problem as follows:\n|_|_|_|_|_|_|_|_ |\nThe '|' bars between the people represent seats. We can think of this problem as arranging the 9 people in the 9 seats. Since we are dealing with a round table, we need to consider this arrangement is the same as the other arrangements where the table is rotated.\nTo count the total number of ways, we can arrange the 9 people in order without considering rotations (permutations of size 9). Using the factorial notation, this can be represented as $9!$.\nHence, there are $\\boxed{362880}$ ways to arrange the 9 people around the round table.The answer is: 362880",
